}
```

LastIndexOf('}') found the class-closing `}`, and I inserted addition + `}` — but I did `$text.Substring(0, $idx) + $addition + "`r`n}"`. Substring(0, idx) keeps everything up to but not including the final `}` — which includes the method's closing `    }`. Hmm wait, but line 262 shows missing `    }`.

Ah — the issue: the file written by part 1 ended with `}\r\n}`? Actually the here-string in part 1 ended with `...isEqualTo(2);\r\n    }\r\n` — the here-string `@'...'@` ends right after the last content line, so the file ends with `    }` (method close) but NO class-closing brace! I forgot to close the class in part 1. Then part 2 appended before the last `}` (which was the method close brace), so methods got nested inside `approvalInvalidationAndPublishBlocking`.

Fix: line 262 should be `    }` before `@Test`. The last `}` of the file is currently the class close? Let me check the end of file. Part 3 also appended the same way. Current structure: ...method2 body, then part2 methods, then part3 methods, then `}`. The `    }` that closed method2 is now at the very end acting as class close, and method2 was never closed. So fix: insert `    }` at line 262 (after `assertThat(...isEqualTo(2);`).

